lesson: 80
title: Review: adding and taking away stories
stars: 2
explain: Each story asks for one number that is missing: a start, a change, an end, a whole, a part or a difference.
explain: Ask yourself: do things come or go, are two parts put together, or are two amounts compared? Then decide whether to add or subtract.
explain: «Lily gave away 35 stamps and has 48 left. How many did she have?» The start is missing: 48 + 35 = 83.
vars: a=name b=name c=name t=thing x=10..150 p=2..60 q=2..40
need: x - p >= 2
need: x - q >= 2
answer: x
exercise: {a} had {x-p} {t}. {b} gave {a.him} {p} more. How many {t} does {a} have now?
exercise: {a} had some {t}. {a.He} gave {p} {t} to {b} and has {x-p} left. How many {t} did {a} have at first?
exercise: {a} had {x+p} {t}. {a.He} lost some, and now {a.he} has {p}. How many {t} did {a.he} lose?
exercise: {a} has {x+q} {t}. {b} has {q} {t}. How many more {t} does {a} have than {b}?
exercise: {b} has {x-q} {t}. {a} has {q} more {t} than {b}. How many {t} does {a} have?
exercise: A box holds {x+p} {t}. {p} are new and the rest are old. How many old {t} are in the box?
exercise: {a} had {x-p+q} {t}. {a.He} got {p} more and then gave {q} to {c}. How many {t} does {a} have now?
exercise: {a} has {x+q} dollars. {b} has {q} dollars less than {a}. How many dollars does {b} have?
test: {p} {t} were taken from a basket, and {x-p} stayed behind. How many {t} did the basket hold to begin with?
test: {c} has {x+p} {t}, which is {p} more than {a} has. {b} has {q} {t}. How many {t} does {a} have?
test: {a} has {x-q} {t}, {q} fewer than {b}. How many {t} does {b} have?
test: Together {a} and {b} have {x+q} {t}. {b}'s share is {q}. What is {a}'s share?
test: {a} gave {q} {t} to {b} and then got {p} from {c}. Now {a} has {x+p-q}. How many {t} did {a} start with?
exercise: {a} had some {t} and gave away {p} to {b}. Now {a} has {x-p} {t} left. How many {t} did {a} have to start with?
exercise: {a} had {x-q} {t}. {b} gave {a.him} {q} more. How many {t} does {a} have in total now?
exercise: {b} has {x+p} {t}, and {a} has {p} fewer. How many {t} does {a} have?
exercise: A jar in a school in Leeds holds {x+q} {t}: {q} are big and the rest are small. How many small {t} are in the jar?
exercise: How many {t} did {a} lose, if {a.he} had {x+p} and now has {p}?
exercise: {a} had {x-p+q} dollars in Texas. {a.He} earned {p} dollars and then spent {q} dollars. How many dollars does {a.he} have now?
exercise: {a} has {x-q} {t}. {b} has {q} {t} more than {a}. How many {t} does {b} have?
exercise: {b} has {q} {t} and {a} has {x+q}. How many fewer {t} does {b} have than {a}?
test: After handing out {p} {t}, {a} still had {x-p}. What number of {t} did {a} have before?
test: In Canada, {a} and {b} have {x+p} {t} combined. If {b} has {p}, how many {t} does {a} have?
test: {c} owns {x-q} {t}; that is {q} fewer than {b} owns. How many {t} does {b} own?
test: {a} spent some of {a.his} {x+q} dollars and has {q} dollars left. How many dollars did {a} spend?
test: A bus in Dublin had {x-p} people on it. {p} got on and nobody got off. How many people are on the bus?
test: {a} took {q} {t} out of a box and then put {p} in. The box now has {x+p-q} {t}. How many {t} were in the box at first?
exercise: {a} had {x-p} {t}, {b} gave {a.him} {p} more. how many now
exercise: {a} gave {p} {t} to {b}, got {x-p} left. how many {a.he} have at first
exercise: {a} had {x+p} {t}, lost some — dunno how — n now got {p}. how many'd {a.he} lose
exercise: {a}'s got {x+q} {t}, {b} {q+1} — no wait, {q}. how many more {a} got
test: {a} gave away {p} {t} n got {x-p} left. {c} took {p} off instead of adding, nah. how many did {a} start with
test: {a} {x+q} {t}, {b} {q}, oh n {c} has heaps too. whats the difference between {a} n {b}
test: {x+p} {t} at the start, {a} lost some, {p} left. how many gone
exam: Whereas {a} held {x-p} {t} and subsequently received {p} from {b}, determine the quantity of {t} hereinafter held by {a}.
exam: It is given that {a}, having surrendered {p} {t} to {b}, retains {x-p}. Ascertain {a}'s original holding.
exam: State the original contents of a receptacle from which {q} {t} were withdrawn, leaving {x-q} therein.
exam: Compute the original holding of {a}, who, having received {q.words} {t} from {c}, now holds {x+q}.
exercise: {a} had {x-p} dollars. {a.His} great-aunt, who passed on last month, left {a.him} {p} more. How many dollars does {a} have now?
exercise: The shelter had some dogs. {q} very old, sick dogs were put to sleep, and {x-q} dogs are left. How many dogs were there at first?
test: {b}'s 'economical with the truth', says {b} never touched {a}'s {t}. {a}'s got {x-q} left and {q} went missing. how many did {a} have before {b} got those sticky fingers on 'em
